---
// Pearl › 03 — The Architecture Call (Figma 189:2876): label, headline and lead in the narrow
// column, the four-file list, two columns of paragraphs, then (wide) a stat strip and the file
// diagram.
//
// The section sits in the wide band; the text is held to the 740 column inside it.
// The diagram is a 972 × 607.6 canvas (`--u` is one Figma pixel) scaled to the column width:
// the blurred backdrop, then the 675 × 512 artwork rebuilt from its Figma layers (the image
// ring, the "Foundation" pearl, its three connector lines and three chips). Layer positions
// are Figma's, with blur and rotation outsets already applied.
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Section from './Section.astro';
import MobileIcon from '../../assets/icons/pearl/mobile.svg';
import LibraryIcon from '../../assets/icons/pearl/library-add-check.svg';
import DesktopIcon from '../../assets/icons/pearl/desktop-mac.svg';
import backdrop from '../../assets/images/pearl/05_section-03-architecture-call__rectangle-18099.png';
import ringImage from '../../assets/images/pearl/06_section-03-architecture-call__rectangle-18098.png';
import ringMask from '../../assets/images/pearl/architecture-call/ring-mask.svg?url';
import ellipse74 from '../../assets/images/pearl/architecture-call/ellipse-74.svg?url';
import ellipse75 from '../../assets/images/pearl/architecture-call/ellipse-75.svg?url';
import ellipse76 from '../../assets/images/pearl/architecture-call/ellipse-76.svg?url';
import ellipse77 from '../../assets/images/pearl/architecture-call/ellipse-77.svg?url';
import ellipse78 from '../../assets/images/pearl/architecture-call/ellipse-78.svg?url';
import ellipse79 from '../../assets/images/pearl/architecture-call/ellipse-79.svg?url';
import ellipse80 from '../../assets/images/pearl/architecture-call/ellipse-80.svg?url';
import line3 from '../../assets/images/pearl/architecture-call/line-3.svg?url';
import line4 from '../../assets/images/pearl/architecture-call/line-4.svg?url';
import line5 from '../../assets/images/pearl/architecture-call/line-5.svg?url';

const files = [
  { name: 'Foundation', note: 'primitives and semantic tokens shared by everything' },
  { name: 'Icon library', note: 'brand icons for brand moments, a utility set for everything else' },
  { name: 'Mobile component library' },
  { name: 'Web component library' },
];

const stats = [
  { value: '4', label: 'Files' },
  { value: '1', label: 'Owner' },
  { value: '3', label: 'Surface' },
];

// The pearl's layers, bottom to top: src, left, top, width, height (Figma px), rotation.
const pearl = [
  { src: ellipse74, x: 258.77, y: 202.58, w: 151.147, h: 149.826 },
  { src: ellipse75, x: 244.36, y: 183.39, w: 181.22, h: 133.503 },
  { src: ellipse78, x: 255.05, y: 262.64, w: 183.856, h: 119.909, r: 180 },
  { src: ellipse80, x: 263.29, y: 308.53, w: 138.681, h: 49.926, r: 180 },
  { src: ellipse77, x: 280.92, y: 211.83, w: 106.678, h: 101.887 },
  { src: ellipse76, x: 255.43, y: 194.47, w: 159.062, h: 111.345 },
  { src: ellipse79, x: 267.68, y: 183.39, w: 133.13, h: 107.036 },
];

// Connector lines, centred on their Figma boxes and rotated into place.
const lines = [
  { src: line3, x: 258.64, y: 125.69, w: 152.202, r: -90 },
  { src: line4, x: 146.87, y: 365.87, w: 144.652, r: 140.03 },
  { src: line5, x: 376.97, y: 365.87, w: 143.443, r: -139.61 },
];
---

<Section tone="pearl" width="wide" labelledby="architecture-title">
  <div class="column">
    <div class="heading">
      <p class="text-label-m label">The architecture call</p>
      <h2 id="architecture-title">
        <span class="line">Four files, <span class="muted">not one,</span></span>
        <span class="line">and a reason for each</span>
      </h2>
    </div>

    <div class="body">
      <p class="text-body-xl">
        Keeping everything in one file would have been simpler at the start. But one file holding
        three platforms would only get harder to manage as the product grew, so I split Pearl into
        four, each with one job.
      </p>

      <ol class="files">
        {files.map(({ name, note }, i) => (
          <li class="file">
            <span class="text-title-m index" aria-hidden="true">{String(i + 1).padStart(2, '0')}</span>
            <p class="text-body-m">
              <span class="text-title-m name">{name}</span>{note && ` - ${note}`}
            </p>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ol>

      <div class="columns text-body-xl text-body-l-mobile">
        <div class="col">
          <p>
            Mobile and web got their own libraries because they behave differently. Web needed
            hover and focus states, mobile needed touch states, and keeping them apart meant each
            could grow without affecting the other.
          </p>
          <p>
            The icon library needed a decision of its own. Batelco’s icon set had scaling issues,
            and we only had access to part of it. At first, filling the gaps meant digging through
            their Confluence for missing icons, which was eating into design time. So I raised it
            through our PM, and we agreed to use Material icons wherever Batelco’s were missing.
            From there, my aim was to keep Batelco’s icons for brand moments and let Material carry
            the everyday utility ones.
          </p>
        </div>
        <p>
          Where Pearl lived got tested too. The client had started keeping foundations in their own
          Figma, and partway through they asked for one unified system instead of one on each side.
          I talked it through with my design head and our PM, then explained our reasoning to the
          client. Our side was producing the larger share of the UI, and keeping the system where
          that UI was being built made it far easier to maintain as the project grew. Pearl stayed
          with us during the build, and at handoff it moved into their environment.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <dl class="stats">
    {stats.map(({ value, label }) => (
      <div class="stat">
        <dt class="text-label-l">{label}</dt>
        <dd class="text-number-xl">{value}</dd>
      </div>
    ))}
  </dl>

  <figure class="figure">
    <div class="panel" role="img" aria-label="Pearl's four files: Foundation at the centre, connected to the icon library (brand and utility icons), web components (133) and mobile components (117).">
      <Image class="backdrop" src={backdrop} alt="" widths={[972, 1372]} sizes="(min-width: 1200px) 972px, 100vw" />

      <div class="artwork" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="ring" style={`mask-image: url("${ringMask}")`}>
          <Image src={ringImage} alt="" widths={[745, 1200]} sizes="(min-width: 1200px) 745px, 80vw" />
        </div>

        <div class="chip" style="--x: 476.39; --y: 413.08">
          <span class="chip-icon"><MobileIcon /></span>
          <span class="chip-text"><span class="chip-title">Mobile components</span>117 components</span>
        </div>
        <div class="chip" style="--x: 235.82; --y: 0">
          <span class="chip-icon"><LibraryIcon /></span>
          <span class="chip-text"><span class="chip-title">Icon library</span>Brand + Utility icons</span>
        </div>
        <div class="chip" style="--x: 0; --y: 413.08">
          <span class="chip-icon"><DesktopIcon /></span>
          <span class="chip-text"><span class="chip-title">Web components</span>133 components</span>
        </div>

        {pearl.map(({ src, x, y, w, h, r = 0 }) => (
          <img class="layer" src={src} alt="" style={`--x: ${x}; --y: ${y}; --w: ${w}; --h: ${h}; --r: ${r}deg`} />
        ))}
        <span class="foundation">Foundation</span>

        {lines.map(({ src, x, y, w, r }) => (
          <img class="layer" src={src} alt="" style={`--x: ${x}; --y: ${y}; --w: ${w}; --h: 4.2205; --r: ${r}deg`} />
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </figure>
</Section>

<style>
  /* Narrow column (740, no side padding in Figma) centred in the wide band. */
  .column {
    max-width: 740px;
    margin-inline: auto;
  }

  .heading {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-24);
  }

  .label {
    color: var(--text-tertiary);
  }

  h2 {
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }

  /* Two lines from tablet up, as in Figma; on mobile it wraps naturally. */
  @media (min-width: 768px) {
    .line {
      display: block;
    }
  }

  .muted {
    color: var(--text-light);
  }

  .body {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-24);
    margin-top: var(--space-32);
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  /* Figma radius 10, snapped to rounded.sm. */
  .files {
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    list-style: none;
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    background-color: var(--bg-cards);
  }

  .file {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: var(--space-16);
    padding: var(--space-16) var(--space-24);
  }

  .index {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    color: var(--text-light);
  }

  .name {
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }

  /* Figma: two columns 24 apart; the left one holds two paragraphs, 24 apart. */
  .columns {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    align-items: start;
    gap: var(--space-24);
  }

  .col {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-24);
  }

  /* Stat strip: 64 below the text, three equal cells. Figma radius 12 snapped to rounded.md. */
  .stats {
    display: flex;
    margin: var(--space-64) 0 0;
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    background-color: var(--bg-cards);
  }

  /* Label sits under the number visually; dt comes first for screen readers. */
  .stat {
    flex: 1;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column-reverse;
    align-items: center;
    gap: var(--space-16);
    padding: var(--space-40) var(--space-32);
  }

  dt {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
  }

  dd {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--text-pearl-tertiary);
  }

  .figure {
    margin-top: var(--space-32);
    container-type: inline-size;
  }

  /* Figma radius 10, snapped to rounded.sm. */
  .panel {
    --u: calc(100cqw / 972);
    position: relative;
    aspect-ratio: 972 / 607.6;
    overflow: hidden;
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm);
    background-color: var(--bg-cards);
  }

  /* Blurred and at 51%, over the white panel, as in Figma. */
  .backdrop {
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
    filter: blur(calc(50 * var(--u)));
    opacity: 0.51;
  }

  .artwork {
    position: absolute;
    left: calc(148 * var(--u));
    top: calc(48 * var(--u));
    width: calc(675.017 * var(--u));
    height: calc(512 * var(--u));
  }

  /* The image, masked to a ring: 469.27 square at 99.71 / 42.73. */
  .ring {
    position: absolute;
    left: calc(99.71 * var(--u));
    top: calc(42.73 * var(--u));
    width: calc(469.267 * var(--u));
    height: calc(469.267 * var(--u));
    overflow: hidden;
    mask-size: 100% 100%;
    mask-repeat: no-repeat;
  }

  .ring img {
    position: absolute;
    left: calc(-140.859 * var(--u));
    top: calc(-143.233 * var(--u));
    width: calc(745.447 * var(--u));
    height: calc(713.793 * var(--u));
    max-width: none;
    object-fit: cover;
  }

  /* Figma chips are Inter 14.24; set in the site font so no extra font loads. */
  .chip {
    position: absolute;
    left: calc(var(--x) * var(--u));
    top: calc(var(--y) * var(--u));
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: calc(9.5 * var(--u));
    padding: calc(9.5 * var(--u)) calc(19 * var(--u)) calc(9.5 * var(--u)) calc(9.5 * var(--u));
    border-radius: var(--radius-full);
    background-color: var(--bg-cards);
    filter: drop-shadow(calc(-6.33 * var(--u)) calc(6.33 * var(--u)) calc(6.33 * var(--u)) rgb(0 0 0 / 0.08));
    color: #141412;
    font-size: calc(14.24 * var(--u));
    line-height: 1.1;
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .chip-icon {
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    width: calc(31.65 * var(--u));
    height: calc(31.65 * var(--u));
    border-radius: var(--radius-full);
    background-color: var(--text-pearl);
  }

  .chip-icon :global(svg) {
    width: calc(19 * var(--u));
    height: calc(19 * var(--u));
  }

  .chip-text {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: calc(3.17 * var(--u));
  }

  .chip-title {
    font-weight: var(--weight-medium);
  }

  .layer {
    position: absolute;
    left: calc(var(--x) * var(--u));
    top: calc(var(--y) * var(--u));
    width: calc(var(--w) * var(--u));
    height: calc(var(--h) * var(--u));
    max-width: none;
    rotate: var(--r);
  }

  /* Figma: JetBrains Mono 12.66, 12% tracking; set in the site font. */
  .foundation {
    position: absolute;
    left: calc(334.34 * var(--u));
    top: calc(269.06 * var(--u));
    translate: -50% 0;
    color: #0F0F0F;
    font-size: calc(12.66 * var(--u));
    font-weight: var(--weight-medium);
    line-height: normal;
    letter-spacing: 0.12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  /* Tablet: the stat strip keeps its row; padding tightens. */
  @media (max-width: 1199px) {
    .stat {
      padding-inline: var(--space-16);
    }
  }

  /* Mobile: paragraphs stack, stats stack centred, the diagram scales down whole. */
  @media (max-width: 767px) {
    .body {
      margin-top: var(--space-24);
    }

    .columns {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: var(--space-24);
    }

    .stats {
      flex-direction: column;
      margin-top: var(--space-48);
    }

    .stat {
      gap: var(--space-8);
      padding-block: var(--space-24);
    }

    .figure {
      margin-top: var(--space-24);
    }
  }
</style>
